==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Crazed M. Titan Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Manic Jamiera Cat''' when obtained from [[Resident Feline (Deadly)|Titan Maniac]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
With his high health and strong area attacks, Crazed Titan Cat is not much different from the [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]]. He can tank hits against long-range or wave enemies such as [[Assassin Bear]], [[Daboo of the Dead]] and [[Berserkory]] while dealing decent damage.

He has much higher initial stats than [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]], which makes a level 50 Manic Jamiera Cat almost equal, in both health and attack power, to a level 20+80 [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]]. Crazed Titan Cat's powerful Lv.10 wave gives it the potential to be a strong frontline damage dealer. That said, a 10-15% wave chance is really low and the long foreswing may cause the attacks to miss anyway. In comparison, [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]]'s 30% chance to [[Knockback|knockback]] non-[[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies and a shorter attack animation tend to make him the more reliable option of the two, unless the use of knockback is not feasible, such as against [[Lowkey]].

